implementationPlan.description:
MoeDaemonClient.releaseTask gains an optional force, and wire-parity.test.cjs pins the frame.
(a) moe-vscode/src/services/MoeDaemonClient.ts, releaseTask only (:1226-1240): signature `releaseTask(taskId: string, reason?: string, force?: boolean): boolean`, payload type `{ taskId: string; reason?: string; force?: true }`, and AFTER the existing reason branch add `if (force === true) { payload.force = true; }`. Strict `=== true` mirrors the daemon (packages/moe-daemon/src/server/WebSocketServer.ts:738-748 forwards `message.payload.force === true`). Appending after reason keeps JetBrains MoeCommandSender.releaseTask's key order (taskId, reason, force), so a plain frame stays byte-identical (A1/A2 pin it). Rewrite the doc comment's last sentence ("`force` is never sent") to say force:true is sent only when force === true: the board's override of a dead holder's step lease (STEP_LEASE_HELD), which TaskDetailPanel asks for after a second confirmation. Touch nothing else in the client: the ERROR case already allowlists context.taskId (:99-115).
(b) moe-vscode/tests/wire-parity.test.cjs: add ONE top-level row right after A4, named exactly `RF7 wire: releaseTask appends force:true after reason only when force is true; any other value sends the plain frame`. Use the file's withClient/connectSocket helpers and compare the RAW strings handed to the socket (sent[i], not parsed):
- ('t1', 'Released from board', true) gives `{"type":"RELEASE_TASK","payload":{"taskId":"t1","reason":"Released from board","force":true}}`;
- ('t1', undefined, true) gives `{"type":"RELEASE_TASK","payload":{"taskId":"t1","force":true}}`;
- each third argument of false, undefined, null, 1, 'true' and {} gives exactly `{"type":"RELEASE_TASK","payload":{"taskId":"t1","reason":"Released from board"}}`;
- a disconnected client with force true returns false and sends nothing.
A1-A4 stay unchanged. Error handling: the sendMessage path is unchanged (false when not connected; a throwing socket still reports through onError, A4). Edit with the seat's own editor (Edit on Claude, apply_patch on codex exec), never a shell write.
